    <briefdescription>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="class_mutable_engine_object" kindref="compound">MutableEngineObject</ref></computeroutput> wrapper that owns a <computeroutput><ref refid="class_homotopy" kindref="compound">Homotopy</ref></computeroutput> via <computeroutput>unique_ptr</computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Mirrors <computeroutput><ref refid="class_m2_s_l_program" kindref="compound">M2SLProgram</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput><ref refid="class_m2_s_l_evaluator" kindref="compound">M2SLEvaluator</ref></computeroutput>: the interpreter handles an opaque <computeroutput>M2Homotopy*</computeroutput> while the templated <computeroutput><ref refid="class_homotopy_concrete" kindref="compound">HomotopyConcrete</ref>&lt;RT, Algorithm&gt;</computeroutput> does the numerical path tracking behind <computeroutput><ref refid="class_m2_homotopy_a368f3085486827b014f3f99e31c025a6_1a368f3085486827b014f3f99e31c025a6" kindref="member">value()</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
